<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Merged over the Info.plist Tauri generates for the macOS bundle. Tauri looks
  for this file in the same directory as `tauri.conf.json` without being told,
  so its presence is the whole wiring.

  One key, for one feature: tone practice records from the microphone, and macOS
  shows this string verbatim in the permission prompt the first time it does.
  A missing `NSMicrophoneUsageDescription` does not fail the build — the app is
  killed at the moment of the request instead, which is why it lives in a file
  that travels with the bundle rather than in a note somewhere.

  The wording is the promise the rest of the app already makes: the audio is
  scored in this process and is never written to disk or sent anywhere.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Hanzi Tutor listens while you hold the button, to check the tone of what you said. The recording is scored on this device and is never saved or sent anywhere.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
